    { version = "2.0.11", text = "See what your party is targeting, and a fix for the ranged swing timer.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Party Frames: |cffffffffParty Targets|r (in the Party section, off by default): a small frame beside each member shows what they are targeting (under each member when the party is horizontal). Click one to target it too. |cffffffffTarget Gap|r sets the space between them, and the |cffffffffTarget|r section has the width, height and border.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Party Frames: the Party section is reordered: Style, Orientation, Sort by Role, Show Player, Pets, Party Targets, then Spacing.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Resource Bars: the |cffffffffRanged Swing|r bar (and the off-hand one) no longer stays hidden when the game hides your attack speed.\n• Tooltips: no more Lua error about a forbidden object when hovering a buff or debuff on an enemy nameplate (fixed in 2.0.10)." },
    { version = "2.0.9", text = "Tidier Edit Mode dialogs, more options back for your frames, and a big clean-up under the hood.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Party Frames: |cffffffffMissing Buffs|r (under Auras, off by default): out of combat, the group buffs a member lacks that you can cast show in the corner across from the buffs.\n• Party Frames: a |cffffffffPet|r section for the pet frames' width, height and border, shown while Pets is on.\n• Boss Frames: a |cffffffffBoss|r section with Growth and a new |cffffffffSpacing|r slider.\n\n|cffffd100Back again|r\n• Cast bars (Player Cast Bar, target, focus, party and boss): |cffffffffHide Icon|r and |cffffffffHide Spell Timer|r; target, focus, party and boss also get |cffffffffCast Bar Height|r, |cffffffffTexture|r and |cffffffffBorder Texture|r.\n• Unit Frames and Party Frames: |cffffffffAbsorb Texture|r and |cffffffffAbsorb Reverse Fill|r in the Look section.\n• Party and Raid Frames: |cffffffffBig Defensive|r and its size; Party Frames: |cffffffffSpacing|r.\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffClean keybind text|r, |cffffffffButton art|r and |cffffffffStop auto-add spells|r.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Edit Mode: every FlareUI frame's dialog uses the same sections in the same order: Frame (Width and Height first), Look (textures), Cast Bar, Auras, Icons. Resource bars have Frame and Look sections too.\n• Damage Meter: it remembers whether you picked Threat or damage, even after a reload. Threat View in Combat goes back to your pick after the fight.\n• Damage Meter: it always shows in Edit Mode, whatever its visibility.\n• Quest Tracker: the default width is 250.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Ability Proc glow: Overpower, Revenge, Execute and the other reaction abilities glow again.\n• Resource Bars: the Fonts tab's text size now changes the bars' text.\n• Tooltips, Damage Meter, Unit Frames and the durability warning: fewer chances of Lua errors from hidden combat values.\n• Status colouring: switching it off clears the grey from your buttons at once.\n• Clean keybind text: switching it off brings Blizzard's labels back without a reload.\n• Chat: the header buttons can no longer flicker between shown and hidden.\n• Addon bag: an addon with both a minimap button and an addon-drawer entry shows once.\n• Radial macros: a macro naming a radial that doesn't exist prints a message instead of an error.\n• Changing unit frame fonts or colours updates raid and boss frames right away." },
